## 2) Brief Justification for Each Service (Project-Specific)

| Service | Why this project uses it |
|---|---|
| Amazon API Gateway | Exposes and secures the frontend APIs (`/child`, `/session/upload`, `/session/{id}/start`, `/session/{id}/insight`, `/feedback`, `/status`) and routes them to `api_handler` Lambda. |
| AWS Lambda | Runs core backend units (`api_handler`, `feature_extraction`, `insight_generator`, `feedback_processor`, `training_check`, `model_trainer`) with autoscaling and no server management. |
| AWS Step Functions | Orchestrates the audio pipeline (`AudioClassifier -> InsightGenerator`) and training pipeline with retries, failure branching, and execution history. |
| Amazon S3 | Stores uploaded audio files, frontend static assets, Terraform remote state, and model artifacts. |
| Amazon DynamoDB | Stores child profile, session records, feedback records, training features, and model versions with low-latency reads/writes. |
| Amazon Cognito | Provides managed sign-in/auth and JWT authorizer integration for API Gateway protected routes. |
| Amazon CloudFront | Delivers the frontend via CDN with HTTPS and caching, reducing origin load and improving response time. |
| Amazon VPC | Keeps Lambda in private subnets, controls egress via NAT, and uses security groups/endpoints for network isolation and safer traffic paths. |
| AWS IAM | Enforces least-privilege permissions between Lambda, Step Functions, S3, DynamoDB, Bedrock, Transcribe, and SageMaker. |
| Amazon ECR | Stores Lambda container images and supports versioned deployments and rollbacks through CI/CD. |
| Amazon CloudWatch | Collects logs and metrics, hosts dashboard, and powers operational alarms for Lambda/API/Step Functions. |
| Amazon SNS | CloudWatch alarms publish to SNS topic; SNS fans out to email/subscribers as a centralized incident notification channel. |
| Amazon EventBridge | Triggers daily training-check execution and supports event-driven pipeline triggering patterns. |
| AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store | Stores runtime references/config (for example, Step Function ARN path) outside application code. |
| Amazon Bedrock | Supports model-based insight text generation path for parent-facing narrative output (when enabled in runtime path). |
| Amazon Transcribe | Performs speech-to-text in linguistic flow (`boto3.client("transcribe")`) so transcript/word analysis can be generated. |
| Amazon SageMaker Serverless Inference | Hosts HuBERT endpoint for Advanced-mode acoustic inference (`boto3.client("sagemaker-runtime")` + endpoint invocation). |
| AWS X-Ray | Captures end-to-end traces across API/Lambda/Step Functions to speed up debugging and latency root-cause analysis. |

